  "id": "COMPOUND:29888 - PROTEIN:4968",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and ZR-75-1, involving a series of enzymatic targets. The compound 2-Methylheptyl propanoate is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the sialylation pathway. This enzyme is then targeted by multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of ZR-75-1, suggesting a potential role for 2-Methylheptyl propanoate in modulating the activity of ZR-75-1 through its interaction with these enzymes. The evidence points to a pathway where 2-Methylheptyl propanoate may influence ZR-75-1 via a series of enzymatic targets, highlighting the importance of sialylation and the role of specific enzymes in the biological process.",
